 void llama_context::sched_alt_select(bool alt) {
+    // Bind the Meta view slot BEFORE the no-op early return.  The slot is `thread_local`, and a thread that runs
+    // two contexts (target + draft head, or the pair's two arms once the speculator is re-admitted) has last
+    // bound whichever context built a graph most recently -- so "the requested state is already the current
+    // state" says nothing about the SLOT.  Rebinding is a thread-local int store; without it the context's
+    // graph is built AND allocated under the other context's view containers, and the Meta backend's view
+    // lookup returns a null tensor for a buffer the two share (`GGML_ASSERT(tensor)` in
+    // ggml_backend_tensor_set_async, measured 2026-11-23: Flash-Next + the external shared MTP head on 3
+    // devices `-sm tensor`, which the r353 delivery build runs and STEP 4 broke).
+    meta_bind_view_slot(alt);
     if (alt == sched_alt_in_use) {
         return;
     }
